Feature: the LIGHT STREAM while skip_draws is on (the emulated GPU stops doing drawing bookkeeping nobody uses)

Applies to: rexglue-sdk nightly-20260921-923c1a59 (thirdparty/rexglue-sdk), after 0004, 0009, 0013, 0015
Apply with: git -C thirdparty/rexglue-sdk apply ../../patches/rexglue-sdk/0021-light-command-stream.patch
Status:     local patch (a feature for our port, not a bug fix)

WHY
  With the port's native renderer showing the game alone (Native Only,
  patch 0009's skip_draws), the emulated GPU draws nothing, but its command
  processor thread still did all the work drawing needs for every register
  write in the stream: the register info lookup (a debug check), shader
  constant dirty marks, texture cache and vertex buffer notes. Plus, every
  time the stream ran dry, 500 yields before sleeping. Measured 2026-11-12
  (the port's `profile 10 <file> GPU Commands`, Wumpa Island, 60 fps):
  the thread used ~29% of a CPU core (81% uncapped, ~4-5 ms of CPU per game
  frame); of its awake time ~75% was register writes, ~25% the idle spin.

WHAT
  New hot-reloadable GPU flag skip_draws_light_stream (default true). While
  skip_draws AND it are on:
  - register writes (type-0/1 packets, SET_CONSTANT, LOAD_*_CONSTANT ranges)
    are only stored in the register file. Registers with side effects outside
    drawing keep the full path: the scratch registers (fences written back to
    memory), COHER_STATUS_HOST, the DC_LUT gamma registers (the port's
    renderer reads the gamma ramp). Decided once per primary buffer.
  - the idle worker sleeps on its event at once (no 500-yield spin).
  - the first draw issued afterwards (F9 back to the emulated picture, or
    the flag turned off) calls the new virtual InvalidateStateAfterLightWrites():
    Vulkan marks every constant buffer out of date, every texture fetch
    constant written and every vertex buffer out of sync, so everything is
    rebuilt from the stored values.
  Not for frames skipped by draw_every_nth_frame (0013): their state is
  needed by the next drawn frame.
  Everything else in the stream runs as before (fences, interrupts, swaps,
  waits), so the game never waits longer.

HOW WE MEASURED IT
  See the port's docs/findings/59-native-only-gpu-thread.md.

